Alembic migration environment for SecureRAG.

The database URL is read from app.core.config (i.e. the DATABASE_URL
environment variable), never from alembic.ini.

Common commands (run from backend/):

  alembic upgrade head            # apply all migrations
  alembic downgrade -1            # roll back one migration
  alembic revision -m "message"   # new empty migration
  alembic current                 # show applied revision

The initial migration is dialect-aware: on PostgreSQL it enables the pgvector
extension and creates HNSW + GIN indexes; on SQLite those steps are skipped and
embeddings are stored as JSON arrays.
